comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T09:18:04.437Z","harness:codex","Fresh audit evidence 2026-08-04: pnpm lint reached the SDK import-cost gate after ESLint, jscpd, static quality, package boundary, package-SDK parity, token budgets, context calibration, gate registry, and SDK surface checks passed. The first fresh-process sample failed governance 536ms>248ms, merge 258ms>195ms, and query 214ms>172ms. An immediate isolated rerun failed on bare node 117ms>95ms instead, demonstrating sample-to-sample and target-to-target instability rather than a stable entrypoint regression. The gate remains a real quality failure until its measurement contract is made robust."
  "2026-08-05T18:27:07.798Z","harness:claude-code","Fresh non-determinism sample, 2026-08-05, on an unchanged src tree (this session's diff touches only scripts/, tests/ and tracker data — zero files under src/). Three consecutive --check runs, back to back, warm cache:\n\n  run 1: Verified SDK entrypoint import costs (10 entrypoints)\n  run 2: FAILED — ./sdk/authoring 140ms > 133ms, ./sdk/query 203ms > 172ms\n  run 3: Verified SDK entrypoint import costs (10 entrypoints)\n\nA prior run in the same session had failed on a different entrypoint again (./sdk 375ms > 367ms). So the gate does not merely false-fail on a cold filesystem cache as the title states — it false-fails on a warm one too, and the entrypoint that trips is not stable between runs. Two of five failures observed today were within 6 percent of the budget.\n\nThat widens the fix: a single-shot fresh-process sample cannot separate an 8ms regression from 8ms of scheduler noise at any cache temperature, so the remedy has to be a sampling and admission policy (best-of-N, or a distribution with a declared confidence), not a warm-up."
  "2026-08-11T14:34:47.393Z","harness:claude-code","Sibling instance observed 2026-08-11, cause not determined. token-budget-gate fails locally on health-default (167 estimated tokens against a 137 budget, baseline 496 bytes / 124 tokens) while the hosted Gates (static) job reports 'Token budget gate passed (29 surfaces checked)' on the identical commit 61d68bd7e. The gate measures an isolated PM_PATH fixture, not the real tracker, so no tracker state can explain it: pm health --check-only emits exactly 496 bytes here through both the global binary and node dist/cli.js, and is byte-identical against a copy of the pre-commit tracker. So the divergence is environmental and reproducible locally, not a flake, and it is not the cold-cache timing shape this item owns - nothing here is timed. Recorded as an adjacent instance rather than filed, because the cause was not isolated. Same class as the closed pm-fr4dg8, where a ratchet verdict turned out to be a property of the working copy rather than of the commit, extended to a gate that reads a synthetic fixture. Anyone re-running this locally should trust the hosted verdict and not update the baseline."
  "2026-08-12T01:18:18.018Z","harness:codex","Fresh reproduction 2026-08-12: two unchanged aggregate pnpm lint runs failed different single samples (./sdk/authoring 147ms > 133ms, then ./sdk/merge 204ms > 195ms); an isolated check immediately passed all ten entrypoints after each failure. This matches the canonical warm-cache nondeterminism and activates the existing sampling fix, without raising budgets."
  "2026-08-12T01:20:05.383Z","harness:codex",Implementation uses the existing five fresh measured processes after one discarded warm-up but admits the median rather than p95/max-of-five. One cold or descheduled outlier no longer false-fails; a majority persistent slowdown still exceeds the unchanged ratchet plus 30ms margin. p95 remains reported as diagnostic evidence and RSS remains max-observed/fail-closed. Focused regression and live ten-entrypoint check pass; budget JSON is unchanged.
  "2026-08-12T01:40:23.138Z","harness:codex","Implementation and verification evidence: SDK entrypoint admission now evaluates the median of five measured cold imports against the unchanged budget plus 30 ms tolerance, while retaining p95 as a diagnostic and maximum RSS as a strict limit. The focused benchmark contract passed 11 tests; repeated isolated gates passed; the aggregate tracker-context pnpm lint passed every static, graph, assurance, token, package, and performance gate; full coverage passed 486 files and 7,242 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-12T02:34:14.857Z","harness:codex","Merged-head evidence: PR #983 merged median-of-five import admission with discarded warm-up, unchanged budgets, diagnostic p95, and strict maximum RSS at 17b40763f. Main CodSpeed run 31556883858 and CI run 31556883969 passed, including static gate and the persistent-regression negative control."
